"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85039896697"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-301aa4d9-8aa9-40dd-85e2-06458f613aaf"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Who designs the ‘Smart City’? An argument for democratising Big Data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381976","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"User centered design (UCD) provides principles and activities for improving usability. However, traditional UCD methods lack considering the context of users in low income, culturally diverse settings and where Information and Communication Technology (ICT) development is at its infant stage. Software development in low and medium income countries like Ethiopia is characterized by big difference in education and livelihood. Heterogeneous cultures both between different ethnic groups and between rural and urban contexts is another challenge for Ethiopian software development. The paper addresses how to adapt UCD methods and agile development to bridge these heterogeneities. To this end, a multi-case study was implemented, researching two projects in an Ethiopian software company. An action research approach has been complemented by a survey and interviews with other companies. It has resulted in contextualization of UCD practices: personas mediated between rural and urban users and developers. Personas helped also customer representatives as well as product owners to understand users and their requirements and allowed to test releases against persona requirements before deployment. Personas were updated throughout the project based on usability testing and experience from early deployment. Besides personas local IT personnel mediated between the rural users and software developers. Pairwise usability testing is an example for cultural adaptation for discount usability evaluation method that has been tried out. Releasing early version to support personnel and members of the company who are closer to the intended users helped to provide a more adapted version from the start.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Teka, Degif","Dittrich, Yvonne","Kifle, Mesfin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382770"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Ethiopia"],"glorg":["Addis Ababa University","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Agile development","Agile methods","Companies","Cultural adaptation","Cultural aspects","Cultural differences","Culture","Discount usability","Ethiopia","Ethiopian software company","Ethiopian software development","Ethnic Groups","Local IT personnel","Personas","Personnel","Scrum","Software Engineering","Testing","UCD methods","UCD practices","Usability","Usability testing","User Centered Design","User Centered Design UCD","User centred design","Workshops","action research approach","culturally diverse settings","discount usability evaluation method","heterogeneous cultures","pairwise usability testing","rural contexts","software developers","urban contexts"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"contextualizing user centered design with agile methods in ethiopia","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82510894/PID4793777.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382770","identifier":[{"id":"85039965785","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6448a213-a497-4600-a274-3d1b1fa18628"],"keyword":["Companies","Cultural differences","Culture","Discount usability","Ethiopia","Ethiopian software company","Ethiopian software development","Local IT personnel","Personas","Personnel","Scrum","Testing","UCD methods","UCD practices","Usability","Usability testing","User Centered Design (UCD)","Workshops","action research approach","agile development","agile methods","cultural adaptation","cultural aspects","culturally diverse settings","discount usability evaluation method","ethnic groups","heterogeneous cultures","pairwise usability testing","rural contexts","software developers","software engineering","urban contexts","user centered design","user centred design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-99C2F96F06297338160150D079875EFC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82510894/PID4793777.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"et","key":"addis ababa university","loc":["Ethiopia","Africa"],"name":"Addis Ababa University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Degif","key":"tekapau","last":"Teka","name":"Teka, Degif","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Y.","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","name_org":"Dittrich, Y.","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mesfin","key":"kiflepau","last":"Kifle","name":"Kifle, Mesfin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/afrcon.2017.8095603","isbn":["9781538627754/17"],"pages":"911-916","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Africon 2017 Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85039965785"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6448a213-a497-4600-a274-3d1b1fa18628"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Contextualizing user centered design with agile methods in Ethiopia","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382770","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"System design and development methods need to be contextualized to the specific needs. Most developing countries are characterized by low economies and infrastructure, complex and heterogeneous culture. In these countries software development is characterized by big differences in education and livelihood. Culture has impacts in ICT development and use. Discount usability methods are lightweight methods to be integrated with agile methods. The paper addresses research questions, what contextual factors in Ethiopia trigger tailoring usability practices, and how can discount usability methods be adapted and integrated into the Scrum-agile development with especial emphasis on the Ethiopian context. The research aims at adapting software engineering and ICT development methods to the specific situation and integrating user-centered design (UCD) and lightweight usability methods into agile development. Two projects have been considered for the empirical research. Cooperative Method Development (CMD) has been used as the research approach. Interview notes, observations and workshop results have been analyzed using thematic coding and qualitative data analysis. Local IT personnel bridged between end users and developers. Culturally adapted user pair testing and heuristic evaluation supported usability testing and supported developers in getting early feedback. Integrated approach of discount usability with the Scrum process has been developed and evaluated first with the involved practitioners and second with expert evaluation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Teka, Degif","Dittrich, Yvonne","Kifle, Mesfin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383663"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Ethiopia"],"glorg":["Addis Ababa University","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Agile methods","Agile software development","Conferences","Cultural differences","Culture","Discount usability","ITU","Local IT personnel","Scrum","Testing","Usability","heuristic evaluation","user pair testing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integrating discount usability in scrum development process in ethiopia","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442854/Integrating_discount_usability_in_scrum_development_process_in_Ethiopia.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383663","identifier":[{"id":"85047249869","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a41c3e50-928d-4b83-8938-56eba0567e29"],"keyword":["Agile methods","Agile software development","Conferences","Cultural differences","ITU","Scrum","Testing","Usability","culture","discount usability","heuristic evaluation","local IT personnel","user pair testing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EDA417AE154ED2A59877609F707D63E0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442854/Integrating_discount_usability_in_scrum_development_process_in_Ethiopia.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"et","key":"addis ababa university","loc":["Ethiopia","Africa"],"name":"Addis Ababa University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Degif","key":"tekapau","last":"Teka","name":"Teka, Degif","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Y.","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","name_org":"Dittrich, Y.","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mesfin","key":"kiflepau","last":"Kifle","name":"Kifle, Mesfin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/iccni.2017.8123811","isbn":["9781509046423"],"pages":"1-8","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2017 International Conference on Computing Networking and Informatics (ICCNI)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85047249869"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a41c3e50-928d-4b83-8938-56eba0567e29"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Integrating discount usability in scrum development process in Ethiopia","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383663","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Information and Communication Technology (ICT) is one of the key enablers for including underserved communities in economic and societal development across the world. Our research analyzes several banking service projects developing technical solutions for rural India. This poster presents an experience report based on systematic debriefing of involved project leaders and initiators, triangulated with additional documentation. The concept of Socio-Technical Prototype is developed and used to show how to mitigate the challenges of ICT based banking service provision for socially constrained communities. The concept of Socio-Technical Prototype extends the notion of prototypes, as it implies a full functioning implementation of the service including all relevant stakeholders. In order to not only prototype end-user functionality but also the interaction of the solution with the specific social, technical and physical environment. The implications for software engineering in the development of such large-scale prototypes and pilots are outlined.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Dittrich, Yvonne","Vaidyanathan, Lakshmi","Gonsalves, Timothy A","Jhunjhunwala, Ashok"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384032"],"event":{"acronym":"ICSE","title":"International Conference on Software Engineering"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South"],"country":["India"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Indian Institute of Technology Madras","Indian Institute of Technology Mandi","Jivass Technologies,"],"keyword":["Information and communication technology ICT","Rural Banking Services","Socio Economic Development","Socio Technical Prototypes","Software Engineering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"developing e banking services for rural india making use of socio technical prototypes","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82429074/Poster_for_ICSEv0.2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384032","identifier":[{"id":"85026770639","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-bd31f438-a30d-407a-b391-2fe9490c8d3e"],"keyword":["Information and Communication Technology (ICT)","Rural Banking Services","Socio-Economic Development","Socio-Technical Prototypes","Software Engineering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4AC81709F28B9637BAF18AB3DB0C8A79"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82429074/Poster_for_ICSEv0.2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"in","key":"jivass technologies","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Jivass Technologies,","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"in","key":"indian institute of technology mandi","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Indian Institute of Technology Mandi","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"in","key":"indian institute of technology madras","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Indian Institute of Technology Madras","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lakshmi","key":"vaidyanathanpau","last":"Vaidyanathan","name":"Vaidyanathan, Lakshmi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Timothy A","key":"gonsalvespau","last":"Gonsalves","name":"Gonsalves, Timothy A","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ashok","key":"jhunjhunwalapau","last":"Jhunjhunwala","name":"Jhunjhunwala, Ashok","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icse-c.2017.55","eisbn":["9781538615898"],"isbn":["9781538615904"],"pages":"204-206","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2017 IEEE/ACM 39th International Conference on Software Engineering Companion (ICSE-C)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026770639"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bd31f438-a30d-407a-b391-2fe9490c8d3e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Developing e-banking services for rural India: making use of socio-technical prototypes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384032","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Organisations are looking for new service offers through innovative use of data, often through a Service Design approach. However, current Service Design tools conceal technological aspects of service development like data and datasets. Data can support the design of future services but is often not represented or rendered as a readily workable design material. This paper reports on an early qualitative study of the tools used to work with data and analytics in a medium-sized organisation. The findings identify the current representations of data and data analytics used in the case organisation. We discuss to which extend the available representations of data and data analytics support data-driven service innovation. A comparison of our findings and current Service Design representations show that Service Design lack to represent data as design material. We propose the notion of expansiveness as a criterion to evaluate future data representations for data-driven Service Design.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Seidelin, Cathrine","Dittrich, Yvonne","Grönvall, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381459"],"event":{"acronym":"IRIS","title":"Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Big data","Design Artefacts","Service innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of a need for data representations in service design","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82951845/Identification_of_a_need_for_data_representations_in_Service_Design_IRIS_2017_12.12.17_CS.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381459","ids":["itu-0d049c3a-a9ea-4ce9-8aaf-e19495c97d3a"],"keyword":["Big Data","Design Artefacts","Service Innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CCF0DF6919D4BA4BD32F3567404A210F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82951845/Identification_of_a_need_for_data_representations_in_Service_Design_IRIS_2017_12.12.17_CS.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cathrine","key":"seidelinpau","last":"Seidelin","name":"Seidelin, Cathrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18919863","23873353"],"issn_org":["18919863"],"issue":"10","journal":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","publisher":"Scandinavian Chapter of the Association for Information Systems (AIS) - Scandinavian IRIS","status":"p","title":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universi