{"abstract":"Today, both businesses and public organizations need to be able to innovate and continuously develop their services and processes along with the underpinning IT infrastructure. We argue that End-User Development (EUD) becomes a necessary part of the innovation capability that underpins such service and process innovation. The book chapter presents a meta-analysis of two case studies. The analysis shows how the need for change in both cases brought about an organizationally established sustainable practice of EUD, where empowered employees cooperated with IT professionals in the development and evolution of an IT infrastructure based on flexible technologies. The chapter further discusses how such practices are supported by (participatory) organizational IT management structures and processes. Finally, it discusses how EUD in this way contributes to the innovation capability of the organization. The conclusion points to transferability of the insights gained and provides suggestions for future research.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Dittrich, Yvonne","Bolmsten, Johan","Eriksson, Jeanette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383436"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Malmö University","World Maritime University, Malmö"],"keyword":["End User Development","Flexible Technologies","Innovation capability","Organizational IT Management","Participatory practices"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"end user development and infrastructuring sustaining organizational innovation capabilities","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85037379608","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383436","identifier":[{"id":"85037379608","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-937107f3-e343-4f4b-865c-37cc6f1ca7a8"],"keyword":["End-User Development","Flexible Technologies","Innovation Capability","Organizational IT Management","Participatory Practices"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-318320C4A74B1B0CAE433B54D9A85815"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"world maritime university malmö","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"World Maritime University, Malmö","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Johan","key":"bolmstenpau","last":"Bolmsten","name":"Bolmsten, Johan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette","key":"erikssonpau","last":"Eriksson","name":"Eriksson, Jeanette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fabio","key":"paternòpedh","last":"Paternò","name":"Paternò, Fabio","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Volker","key":"wulfpedh","last":"Wulf","name":"Wulf, Volker","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-60291-2_8","eisbn":["9783319602912"],"isbn":["9783319602905"],"pages":"165-206","place":"Cham","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"New Perspectives in End-User Development"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85037379608"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-937107f3-e343-4f4b-865c-37cc6f1ca7a8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"End User Development and Infrastructuring - Sustaining Organizational Innovation Capabilities","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383436","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"With its rapid proliferation in the developing world, information and communication technology (ICT) has been accepted as an opportunity to assist disadvantaged people. Many projects have piloted ICT supporting rural communities in developing countries. Such rural communities are socially complex and infrastructurally weak environments that demand clear understanding of the social, economical, cultural and political preconditions when implementing ICT innovations. To provide a comprehensive overview of what kinds of ICT intervention and research contributions have been achieved, a systematic mapping study (SMS) was carried out. This work presents the state-of-the-art based on related journal and conference papers published between 2006-2014. The review indicates that ICT supporting farmers has gained attention over the past few years with a growing number of contributions. However, the field is still in a consolidating phase. Theoretical concepts are sparse, so it is difficult to generalize and transfer the findings. Specifically, there is limited research in IT design and development process; user-interface design for illiterate people; and user and community involvement in the design process.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Zewge, Amanuel","Dittrich, Yvonne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383498"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agriculture","Design method","Development","Information systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"systematic mapping study of information technology for development in agriculture the case of developing countries","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/j.1681-4835.2017.tb00602.x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383498","identifier":[{"id":"85028428420","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-97ce009d-a8da-427c-8ded-3322d49dbb1b"],"keyword":["Agriculture","Design Method","Development","Information Systems"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-69E72B7E66A513A2F379FF0B910C5E7B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/j.1681-4835.2017.tb00602.x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83231749/SYSTEMATIC_MAPPING_STUDY_OF_INFORMATION_TECHNOLOGY_FOR.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amanuel","key":"zewgepau","last":"Zewge","name":"Zewge, Amanuel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/j.1681-4835.2017.tb00602.x","issn":["16814835"],"issue":"1","journal":"The Electronic Journal of Information Systems in Developing Countries","pages":"1-25","publisher":"City University of Hong Kong Department of Information Systems","status":"p","title":"The Electronic Journal of Information Systems in Developing Countries","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85028428420"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-97ce009d-a8da-427c-8ded-3322d49dbb1b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Systematic Mapping Study of Information Technology for Development in Agriculture (The Case of Developing Countries)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383498","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Usability is central especially in contexts with highly heterogeneous user groups as it is the case in developing countries. User involvement and participation has positive impacts towards developing usable software and system success and it is one of the core principles in user centered design (UCD). But how does the industry in developing countries work with UCD and usability evaluation? The article reports from a survey on usability evaluation and UCD practices in Ethiopian software organizations. It aims at exploring the practice of usability evaluation, user involvement and participation in the software organizations in Ethiopia. Some part of the survey question is adapted from a previously conducted survey in Italy and Denmark and further expanded with a set of questions referring to user involvement and participation. The survey was triangulated with interviews with a subset of the respondents. The results show that the percentage of organizations performing some form of usability evaluation is low in Ethiopia. The challenges of usability evaluation observed in the study was analyzed with respect to the challenges of ‘digital divide’ against the publicly available methods and practices and among developed and developing nations using real access/ real impact criteria. The result shows that there are some unique challenges of usability not discussed in the literature reviewed in any detail such as less IT skills, lack of trained professionals, and lack of awareness. The result for user involvement shows also some unique challenges: lack of user motivation, acceptance of change and cultural influence. However, more than 80% of the surveyed organizations claim involving users in some kind in product development. The implications of these findings with respect to the need to contextualize UCD and usability methods are discussed.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Teka, Degif","Dittrich, Yvonne","Kifle, Mesfin","Ardito, Carmelo","Lanzilotti, Rosa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-385013"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Ethiopia","Italy"],"glorg":["Addis Ababa University","All Global Affiliations","University of Bari"],"keyword":["Awareness","Context","Culture","Skill","Usability evaluation","User involvement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"user involvement and usability evaluation in ethiopian software organizations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/j.1681-4835.2017.tb00616.x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-385013","identifier":[{"id":"85032392694","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ff6a29db-2313-40b2-b166-df681f337118"],"keyword":["Awareness","Context","Culture","Skill","Usability Evaluation","Usability Evaluation, User Involvement, Awareness, Skill, Context, Culture","User Involvement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-68E09E82D647B45489C42D375360C084"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83231778/Teka_et_al_2017_The_Electronic_Journal_of_Information_Systems_in_Developing_Countries.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/j.1681-4835.2017.tb00616.x","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"et","key":"addis ababa university","loc":["Ethiopia","Africa"],"name":"Addis Ababa University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhage