i, Rafael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Cleidson R. B. de","key":"souzapau","last":"Souza","name":"Souza, Cleidson R. B. de","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anita","key":"sarmapau","last":"Sarma","name":"Sarma, Anita","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandeep","key":"athavalepau","last":"Athavale","name":"Athavale, Sandeep","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icse.2015.309","isbn":["9781479919345"],"pages":"969-970","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"37th IEEE/ACM International Conference on Software Engineering, ICSE 2015, Florence, Italy, May 16-24, 2015, Volume 2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84951776898"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e0acfc17-e38d-4a91-9bbf-4ea16f75e03e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"8th International Workshop on Cooperative and Human Aspects of Software Engineering (CHASE 2015)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384571","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Modern organisations need to be able to adjust to changes in the environment, changes which are ever more rapid, and in doing so capitalise on the creativity and innovations of their employees. As suggested by Boulus-Rødje and Bjørn (Chap. 14), information technology (IT) applications today are likely to take the form of complex, integrated infrastructures, supporting collaboration within and across organisations. This places requirements on the IT infrastructure. As the work practices within an organisation change, the supporting infrastructure also needs to evolve.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bolmsten, Johan","Dittrich, Yvonne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381605"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Collaborative IT infrastructure","Dynamic work practices","Innovation management","Integrated information technology","Organisational adaptability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"organisational it managed from the shop floor developing participatory design on the organisational arena","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-381605","ids":["itu-16353fcd-57bf-4cc4-9da0-efcc2de65c86"],"keyword":["Collaborative IT infrastructure","Dynamic work practices","Innovation management","Integrated information technology","Organisational adaptability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5A049AA3E0E51F2169F0937F0E347079"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Johan","key":"bolmstenpau","last":"Bolmsten","name":"Bolmsten, Johan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-1-4471-6720-4_16","eisbn":["9781447167204"],"isbn":["9781447167198"],"issn":["14311496"],"pages":"383-417","publisher":"Springer","series":"Computer Supported Cooperative Work Series","status":"p","title":"Designing Socially Embedded Technologies in the Real-World","volume":"Part IV"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-16353fcd-57bf-4cc4-9da0-efcc2de65c86"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Organisational IT managed from the shop floor : Developing Participatory Design on the organisational arena","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381605","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Begel, Andrew","Prikladnicki, Rafael","Dittrich, Yvonne","De Souza, Cleidson","Sarma, Anita","Athavale, Sandeep"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381268"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South"],"country":["Brazil"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Federal University of Para","IBM Brazil"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chase 000000000015 proceedings of the eighth international workshop on cooperative and human aspects of software engineering","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-381268","ids":["itu-0136ec95-c26b-4775-a133-3aeacaa26b76"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1F3E3808F06F9803312820D6970ECBEE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"br","key":"ibm brazil","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"IBM Brazil","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"br","key":"federal university of para","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Federal University of Para","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew","key":"begelped","last":"Begel","name":"Begel, Andrew","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rafael","key":"prikladnickiped","last":"Prikladnicki","name":"Prikladnicki, Rafael","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichped","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Cleidson","key":"desouzaped","last":"De Souza","name":"De Souza, Cleidson","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anita","key":"sarmaped","last":"Sarma","name":"Sarma, Anita","rank":5,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandeep","key":"athavaleped","last":"Athavale","name":"Athavale, Sandeep","rank":6,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0136ec95-c26b-4775-a133-3aeacaa26b76"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"CHASE '15: Proceedings of the Eighth International Workshop on Cooperative and Human Aspects of Software Engineering","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381268","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Context: A rural community in a developing country is a socially complex and infrastructural weak environment that demands clear understanding of the social, economical, cultural, and political precondition before implementing information commutation technology (ICT) innovations. Objective: This work aims to conduct a Systematic Mapping Study (SMS) to get an in-depth understanding about ICT based researches for agriculture in developing countries. Method: A systematic mapping study was carried out to investigate and distill the state-of-the-art from ranked journals and conference publications. In doing so, data extraction task was carried out using fifteen variables. Eg. What kinds of research challenges and contributions were reported to design ICTs based solutions? Which disciplines (knowledge areas) were most explored? Result: ICT in agriculture has gained attention over the past few years with number of contributions but still there is long ways to go. The review shows that currently there are limited knowledge areas in methods, user interface design, and theory in how to design information system for rural community settings. Conclusion: This paper first presents an overview of research topics and trends from selected top ranked ICT4D Journals and conference proceedings. Second, the detailed explanation about the proposed and/ or used frameworks, theoretical underpinning, methods and Technology used were discussed, among others. Third, the paper also motivates others researchers for an ongoing discourse to fill identified gaps from software engineering, computer science or information system research perspective. Keywords: design method, information system, development, agriculture.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Zewge, Amanuel","Dittrich, Yvonne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382033"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agricultural Research","Developing countries","ICT Innovations","Rural Community","Systematic mapping study"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"systematic mapping study of information communication technology research for agriculture in case of developing countries","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80517485/TR_2015_190.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382033","ids":["itu-342e12be-7624-416e-885b-5b829b42cb18"],"keyword":["Agricultural Research","Developing Countries","ICT Innovations","Rural Community","Systematic Mapping Study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4A2388C24CD37945FC5DAF56374CEA24"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80517485/TR_2015_190.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amanuel","key":"zewgepau","last":"Zewge","name":"Zewge, Amanuel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16006100"],"issue":"TR-2015-190","pages":"21","place":"Copenhagen","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","repno":"IT University Technical Report Series, TR-2015-190","series":"IT University Technical Report Series","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-342e12be-7624-416e-885b-5b829b42cb18"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Systematic mapping study of information communication technology research for agriculture (in case of developing Countries)","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382033","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Most of the Information and Communication Technology for Development initiatives introduced to communities in developing countries fails to deliver its promises due to the lack of intended beneficiary involvement. Participatory Design assumes to be effective as long as its nature of participations and methods are contextualized to a given settings. To this end, we discuss the implication of considering local (rural community) culture of participation practices, and propose a procedure to be followed in the early phases of information system development process. Finally we argue that, such adaption could advance the Participatory Action Research methodology.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Zewge, Amanuel","Dittrich, Yvonne","Bekele, Rahel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382963"],"event":{"end":"2015-09-17","place":"Addis Ababa, et","start":"2015-09-14","title":"IEEE AFRICON","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agriculture","Collaborative work","Context","Cultural differences","Design methodology","Information Commuication Technology for Development","Information systems","Participatory design Agriculture","Stakeholders"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adapting participatory design to design information system with rural ethiopian community","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84962597706","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382963","identifier":[{"id":"84962597706","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-728d593c-9764-4eb9-8ae9-b18f71a18f2d"],"keyword":["Agriculture","Collaborative work","Context","Cultural differences","Design methodology","Information Commuication Technology for Development","Information systems","Participatory design Agriculture","Stakeholders"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E92BDC4A1AA6D2E9AE49312A13694535"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amanuel","key":"zewgepau","last":"Zewge","name":"Zewge, Amanuel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rahel","key":"bekelepau","last":"Bekele","name":"Bekele, Rahel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/afrcon.2015.7331974","isbn":["9781479974986"],"pages":"1-5","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"AFRICON, 2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84962597706"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-728d593c-9764-4eb9-8ae9-b18f71a18f2d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Adapting participatory design to design information system with rural Ethiopian community","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382963","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Current literature on urban planning explores how to use ICT to support citizen participation. Advances in open data and its possibility to easily represent data on maps, opens up new opportunities to support participation and decision making in urban projects. This article investigates how spatial planners today use data to inform the participatory process. Looking at the participation process as collaboration between planners and citizens allows us to see the participation process itself as generating data that informs future decisions and processes. Based on a case study of a participatory process of an urban renewal project, the article investigates the use of structured and unstructured data for participation. The fieldwork is conducted using ethnographically inspired methods, based on participatory observations, interviews and document analysis. As a result, the incremental decisions, the resulting process, and the data used in this process are mapped out. Besides the need to accommodate heterogeneous data and to allow for integrated analysis of data specific to the neighborhood under development, the important result is that the participatory process itself generates data that informs the further process and the decisions that are part of it. The paper concludes with design implications for decision support for urban planning. In future research, the intention is to explore these implications in a Participatory Design process.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ddamba, Joshua","Dittrich, Yvonne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382510"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Participatory Design","Urban planning","Urban renewal","Visualisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data for participation and participation as data supporting incremental participatory decision making in urban planning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81825722/Data_for_Participation_Participaton_as_Data_Joshua_Yvonne_Final_IRIS_Submission.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382510","ids":["itu-52d0adae-04a5-4dbb-80d0-311c037a0a3d"],"keyword":["Participatory Design","Urban Planning","Urban Renewal","Visualisation,"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3711037F41B73E97C60CFD0B1040A0B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81825722/Data_for_Participation_Participaton_as_Data_Joshua_Yvonne_Final_IRIS_Submission.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joshua","key":"ddambapau","last":"Ddamba","name":"Ddamba, Joshua","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18919863","23873353"],"issn_org":["18919863"],"issue":"6","journal":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","publisher":"Scandinavian Chapter of the Association for Information Systems (AIS) - Scandinavian IRIS","status":"p","title":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","volume":"2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-52d0adae-04a5-4dbb-80d0-311c037a0a3d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Data for Participation and Participation as Data: Supporting Incremental Participatory Decision-Making in Urban Planning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382510","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In Global Software Development (GSD) the lack of face-to-face communication is a major challenge and effective computer-mediated practices are necessary to mitigate the effect of physical distance. Communication through Social Software (SoSo) supports team coordination, helping to deal with geographical distance; however, in Software Engineering literature, there is a lack of suitable theoretical concepts to analyze and describe everyday practices of globally-distributed software development teams and to study the role of communication through SoSo. The paper proposes a theoretical framework for analyzing how communicative and coordinative practices are constituted and maintained in globally-distributed teams. Method. The framework is based on the concepts of communicative genres and coordination mechanisms; it is motivated and explicated through examples from two qualitative empirical cases. Coordination mechanisms and communicative genres mutually support each other. In particular, communication through SoSo supports team members in establishing, developing and maintaining social protocols within the distributed team. Software Engineering tools and methods provide templates for coordination mechanism that need to be adapted and adopted in order to support the project at hand. SoSo serves as a medium for the necessary metawork. The theoretical framework proposed is used to describe both the practices in an established industrial project and the establishing of practices in three student teams. The framework allows explaining the heterogeneity of practices observed. This paper presents a conceptual framework to study the role of communication through SoSo for coordination in GSD. The usefulness of the framework is supported by empirical findings on the role of SoSo. The theoretical framework can be beneficial for future research that aims to analyze and describe not only the role of SoSo, but also how communicative and coordinative practices can be established and maintained in GSD teams.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Giuffrida, Rosalba","Dittrich, Yvonne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383351"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Communicative genres","Coordination mechanisms","Global Software Development","Human Aspects","Social Software"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a conceptual framework to study the role of communication through social software for coordination in globally distributed software teams","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81831959/conceptualFramework.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383351","identifier":[{"id":"84928139330","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8dd9d27f-4592-4960-8555-9396884a8efc"],"keyword":["Communicative genres","Coordination mechanisms","Global software development","Human aspects","Social software"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DC86BE918BB37799AD548DD44722A4D7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81831959/conceptualFramework.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosalba","key":"giuffridapau","last":"Giuffrida","name":"Giuffrida, Rosalba","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.infsof.2015.02.013","issn":["09505849","18736025"],"issn_org":["09505849"],"journal":"Information and Software Technology","pages":"11-30","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Information and Software Technology","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84928139330"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8dd9d27f-4592-4960-8555-9396884a8efc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A conceptual framework to study the role of communication through social software for coordination in globally-distributed software teams","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383351","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Integration of human-centered design in a company's software development practice requires a thorough analysis of its current practices by both researchers and practitioners.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ardito, Carmelo","Buono, Paolo","Caivano, Danilo","Costabile, Maria Francesca","Lanzilotti, Rosa","Dittrich, Yvonne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381383"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bari"],"keyword":["Action research","Human centered design","Software development","Usability","cooperative method development","software technologies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"human centered design in industry lessons from the trenches","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84919909203","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381383","identifier":[{"id":"84919909203","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-084936af-33c6-4df5-8e4a-d0b404e20059"],"keyword":["action research","cooperative method development","human-centered design","software development","software technologies","usability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8166B9CE026A5726A8977B4CE2DB8416"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of bari","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bari","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carmelo","key":"arditopau","last":"Ardito","name":"Ardito, Carmelo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"buonopau","last":"Buono","name":"Buono, Paolo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Danilo","key":"caivanopau","last":"Caivano","name":"Caivano, Danilo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Francesca","key":"costabilepau","last":"Costabile","name":"Costabile, Maria Francesca","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosa","key":"lanzilottipau","last":"Lanzilotti","name":"Lanzilotti, Rosa","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00189162","15580814"],"issn_org":["00189162"],"issue":"12","journal":"Computer","pages":"86-89","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Computer","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84919909203"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-084936af-33c6-4df5-8e4a-d0b404e20059"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Human-Centered Design in Industry: Lessons from the Trenches","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381383","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Information and Communication Technology (ICT) is more and more promoted as a driver and facilitator of economic growth and development in low and middle income countries. ICT for Development (ICT4D) though has mixed successes. Sustainability of solutions and usability respectively usefulness for the intended beneficiaries have been reported as causes. Participatory approaches to development have been proposed to address these causes. Participatory Design (PD) seems like a perfect fit. However, at the Participatory Design Conferences, research that addresses PD in low and middle income countries is rare. The workshop aims at bringing together the PD researchers working with under-privileged communities and attracting researchers from the ICT4D communities to the PD conference. The goal is to share experiences and start a discussion on how participation, ICT and development might relate.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Dittrich, Yvonne","De La Harpe, Retha","Korpela, Mikko","Macueve, Gertrudes","Bekele, Rahel","Kaasbøll, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384198"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["ICT4D participative development participatory design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"participation for development","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2662155.2662207","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384198","identifier":[{"id":"85011878147","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c7e35659-b5ec-4241-a4d6-fce4e0060d5c"],"keyword":["ICT4D, participative development, participatory design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6EC558AA382E1F82BE87E51E0E0812A9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://doi.acm.org/10.1145/2662155.2662207","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2662155.2662207","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Retha","key":"delaharpepau","last":"De La Harpe","name":"De La Harpe, Retha","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikko","key":"korpelapau","last":"Korpela","name":"Korpela, Mikko","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gertrudes","key":"macuevepau","last":"Macueve","name":"Macueve, Gertrudes","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rahel","key":"bekelepau","last":"Bekele","name":"Bekele, Rahel","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"kaasbøllpau","last":"Kaasbøll","name":"Kaasbøll, Jens","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2662155.2662207","isbn":["9781450332149"],"pages":"213-214","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 13th Participatory Design Conference: Short Papers, Industry Cases, Workshop Descriptions, Doctoral Consortium Papers, and Keynote Abstracts - Volume 2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85011878147"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c7e35659-b5ec-4241-a4d6-fce4e0060d5c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Participation for Development","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384198","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In a developing country like Ethiopia, marketing of agricultural products is influenced by local, socioeconomic, cultural and IT infrastructure characteristics. ICT-based agriculture information systems have been proposed to support farmers with market information. However, such initiatives have often failed to provide useful information in an adequate form for farmers in remote areas. Participatory Design (PD) assumes to be effective approach to overcome these challenges. However, due to its origin in the western countries, the capability of users, motivation and desire to participate and availability of resources are often taken for granted. This work identifies challenges for applying PD in rural Ethiopia and proposes method for ‘Early-Stage’ of PD.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Zewge, Amanuel","Dittrich, Yvonne","Bekele, Rahel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384807"],"event":{"end":"2014-10-05","place":"Windhoek, na","start":"2014-10-05","title":"Participation for Development","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agricultural Marketing","ICT in Agriculture","Participatory Design","Rural Ethiopia","Socioeconomic Influences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"providing market information for ethiopian farmers extending participatory design","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.itu.dk/people/ydi/final/participation4d_submission_8.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384807","ids":["itu-f03e1c80-5e4f-4edd-891a-00eef478ff1a"],"keyword":["Agricultural Marketing","ICT in Agriculture","Participatory Design","Rural Ethiopia","Socioeconomic Influences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CC13BC566CAE9EB4B61D9F79D1836E47"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.itu.dk/people/ydi/final/participation4d_submission_8.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amanuel","key":"zewgepau","last":"Zewge","name":"Zewge, Amanuel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rahel","key":"bekelepau","last":"Bekele","name":"Bekele, Rahel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f03e1c80-5e4f-4edd-891a-00eef478ff1a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Providing Market Information for Ethiopian Farmers: Extending Participatory Design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384807","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The main part of software engineering methods, tools and technologies has developed around projects as the central organisational form of software development. A project organisation depends on clear bounds regarding scope, participants, development effort and lead-time. What happens when these conditions are not given? The article claims that this is the case for software product specific ecosystems. As software is increasingly developed, adopted and deployed in the form of customisable and configurable products, software engineering as a discipline needs to take on the challenge to support software ecosystems. Objective The article provides a holistic understanding of the observed and reported practices as a starting point to device specific support for the development in software ecosystems. Method A qualitative interview study was designed based on previous long-term ethnographical inspired research. Results The analysis results in a set of common features of product development and evolution despite differences in size, kind of software and business models. Design is distributed and needs to be coordinated across heterogeneous design constituencies that, together with the software, build a product specific socio-technical ecosystem. The technical design has to support the deference of part of the development not only to 3rd-party developers but also to local designers tailoring the software in the use organisation. The technical interfaces that separate the work of different design constituencies are contested and need to be maintained permanently. Development takes place as cycles within cycles – overlaying development cycles with different rhythms to accommodate different evolution drivers. Conclusion The reported practices challenge some of the very core assumptions of traditional software engineering, but makes perfect sense, considering that the frame of reference for product development is not a project but continuous innovation across the respective ecosystem. The article provides a number of concrete points for further research.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Dittrich, Yvonne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381980"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Qualitative empirical research","Software ecosystems","Software product development"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"software engineering beyond the project sustaining software ecosystems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.infsof.2014.02.012","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381980","identifier":[{"id":"84905466535","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-30717198-a29b-4345-a2f8-c89c72f8c55b"],"keyword":["Qualitative empirical research","Software ecosystems","Software product development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3563F1ED5C2A83977DDA27925DFD7E08"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.infsof.2014.02.012","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.infsof.2014.02.012","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.infsof.2014.02.012","issn":["09505849","18736025"],"issn_org":["09505849"],"issue":"11","journal":"Information and Software Technology","pages":"1436-1456","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Information and Software Technology","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84905466535"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-30717198-a29b-4345-a2f8-c89c72f8c55b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Software engineering beyond the project : Sustaining software ecosystems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381980","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In Global Software Development (GSD), the lack of face- to-face communication is a major challenge and effective computer-mediated practices are necessary. This paper analyzes cooperative practices supported by Social Software (SoSo) in a GSD student project. The empirical results show that the role of SoSo is to support informal communication, enabling social talks and metawork, both necessary for establishing and for maintaining effective coordination mechanisms, thus successful cooperation.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Giuffrida, Rosalba","Dittrich, Yvonne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382215"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Articulation Work Communicative Genres Coordination Mechanisms Global Software Development Metawork Social Software Socialization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how social software supports cooperative practices in a globally distributed software project","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2593702.2593716","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382215","identifier":[{"id":"84949539043","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-40258493-5244-4641-afb1-657815b599d3"],"keyword":["Articulation Work, Communicative Genres, Coordination Mechanisms, Global Software Development, Metawork, Social Software, Socialization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3138903554A50A1AEF6ED94DD2E9C011"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://doi.acm.org/10.1145/2593702.2593716","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2593702.2593716","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosalba","key":"giuffridapau","last":"Giuffrida","name":"Giuffrida, Rosalba","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2593702.2593716","isbn":["9781450328609"],"pages":"24-31","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 7th International Workshop on Cooperative and Human Aspects of Software Engineering"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84949539043"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-40258493-5244-4641-afb1-657815b599d3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How Social Software Supports Cooperative Practices in a Globally Distributed Software Project","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382215","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"ICT Interventions at agriculture information service provide rural farmer with the knowledge to improve their wellbeing. There are various technological and operational components that go into design of a software system particularly in ICT for development initiatives. We aimed to design method that covers socio-technical issues via participatory design.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Zewge, Amanuel","Dittrich, Yvonne","Bekele, Rahel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382865"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["ICT4D action research design research"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"software designing methodology for ict000000000004d domain","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2662155.2662244","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382865","identifier":[{"id":"85011796738","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6b6016bc-d2ca-4fdc-bf8b-de5016cc9ebf"],"keyword":["ICT4D, action research, design research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B8ABB73C39BFE246B046B853E04ACF38"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://doi.acm.org/10.1145/2662155.2662244","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2662155.2662244","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amanuel","key":"zewgepau","last":"Zewge","name":"Zewge, Amanuel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rahel","key":"bekelepau","last":"Bekele","name":"Bekele, Rahel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2662155.2662244","isbn":["9781450332149"],"pages":"237-241","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 13th Participatory Design Conference: Short Papers, Industry Cases, Workshop Descriptions, Doctoral Consortium Papers, and Keynote Abstracts - Volume 2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85011796738"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6b6016bc-d2ca-4fdc-bf8b-de5016cc9ebf"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Software Designing Methodology for ICT4D Domain","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382865","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The workshop will examine issues around emerging participation in (re-)designing technological and/or societal infrastructures. Contributions should provide cases and/or methodological reflections on connecting ongoing social or professional practices involving infrastructure usages with emerging and/or collaborative processes of changing/improving those infrastructures. Contributions may provide an analytical perspective or methods/tools to stimulate and support processes and activities of infrastructuring.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bossen, Claus","Ehn, Pelle","Karasti, Helena","Di Salvo, Carl","Clement, Andrew","Pipek, Volkmar","Dittrich, Yvonne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384099"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["infrastructure infrastructuring participatory design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infrastructuring collaboration and evolving socio material practices of changing our world","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2662155.2662211","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384099","identifier":[{"id":"85011879230","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c1e05fb4-49a6-42d5-9d8c-372d7ba23e55"],"keyword":["infrastructure, infrastructuring, participatory design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6E3240731BAB60C9FC16706C97406F4E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://doi.acm.org/10.1145/2662155.2662211","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2662155.2662211","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"bossenpau","last":"Bossen","name":"Bossen, Claus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Pelle","key":"ehnpau","last":"Ehn","name":"Ehn, Pelle","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Helena","key":"karastipau","last":"Karasti","name":"Karasti, Helena","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Carl","key":"disalvopau","last":"Di Salvo","name":"Di Salvo, Carl","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew","key":"clementpau","last":"Clement","name":"Clement, Andrew","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Volkmar","key":"pipekpau","last":"Pipek","name":"Pipek, Volkmar","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2662155.2662211","isbn":["9781450332149"],"pages":"221-222","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 13th Participatory Design Conference: Short Papers, Industry Cases, Workshop Descriptions, Doctoral Consortium Papers, and Keynote Abstracts - Volume 2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85011879230"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c1e05fb4-49a6-42d5-9d8c-372d7ba23e55"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Infrastructuring, Collaboration and Evolving Socio-material Practices of Changing Our World","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384099","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Specific, situated participatory design (PD) practices have always been at the heart of Participatory Design research. The role of the very situatedness and specificity of PD practice for theory-building within PD research is, however, seldom discussed explicitly. In this article, we explore why and in which ways the specificity and situatedness of PD practices are crucial for PD research. We do so by developing the notion of PD as situated innovation based on a pragmatic epistemology. PD research aims at devel oping and continuously unfolding what PD can, might and should be. We show implications of such a pragmatic epistemology of PD on understanding and arguing for PD research approaches. These concepts are illustrated referring to PD practices as experienced in PD research projects. Our epistemological argumentation supports the emphasis on exploring new PD practices and learning and theorizing about PD from the specificities, in line with recent debate contributions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Dittrich, Yvonne","Eriksén, Sara","Wessels, Bridgette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382533"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Blekinge Institute of Technology","University of Sheffield"],"keyword":["Epistemology","Participatory Design","Pragmatism","situated innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"learning through situated innovation why the specific is crucial for participatory design research","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://aisel.aisnet.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1251&context=sjis","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382533","identifier":[{"id":"84906519155","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-549d76f5-9e72-47ac-b46b-1166e29fd1dd"],"keyword":["Participatory design","epistemology","pragmatism","situated innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-B5406BE27520B0529C30C09780605E75"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://aisel.aisnet.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1251&context=sjis","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"blekinge institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Blekinge Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of sheffield","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sheffield","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"eriksénpau","last":"Eriksén","name":"Eriksén, Sara","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bridgette","key":"wesselspau","last":"Wessels","name":"Wessels, Bridgette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09050167"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Information Systems","pages":"29-56","publisher":"Aalborg Universitet","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Information Systems","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84906519155"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-549d76f5-9e72-47ac-b46b-1166e29fd1dd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Learning through Situated Innovation : Why the specific is crucial for Participatory Design Research","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382533","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Dittrich, Yvonne","Burnett, Margaret M.","Mørch, Anders I.","Redmiles, David F."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381615"],"event":{"end":"2013-06-13","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2013-06-10","title":"International Symposium on End-User Development","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"end user development 000000000004th international symposium is eud 000000002013 copenhagen denmark june 000000000010 000000000013 000000002013 proceedings","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-381615","ids":["itu-170e24b3-ccdd-45cb-be20-80aaa605cc79"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EC538FBB87C4CA2DD379D11340EAE06C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichped","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Margaret M.","key":"burnettped","last":"Burnett","name":"Burnett, Margaret M.","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders I.","key":"mørchped","last":"Mørch","name":"Mørch, Anders I.","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"David F.","key":"redmilesped","last":"Redmiles","name":"Redmiles, David F.","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9783642387050"],"issn":["03029743"],"publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-170e24b3-ccdd-45cb-be20-80aaa605cc79"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"End-User Development - 4th International Symposium, IS-EUD 2013, Copenhagen, Denmark, June 10-13, 2013. Proceedings","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381615","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Background: In Global Software Development (GSD), informal communication and knowledge sharing play an important role. Social Software (SoSo) has the potential to support and foster this key responsibility. Research on the use of SoSo in GSD is still at an early stage: although a number of empirical studies on the usage of SoSo are available in related fields, there exists no comprehensive overview of what has been investigated to date across them. Objective: The aim of this review is to map empirical studies on the usage of SoSo in Software Engineering projects and in distributed teams, and to highlight the findings of research works which could prove to be beneficial for GSD researchers and practitioners. Method: A Systematic Mapping Study is conducted using a broad search string that allows identifying a variety of studies which can be beneficial for GSD. Papers have been retrieved through a combination of automatic search and snowballing, hence a wide quantitative map of the research area is provided. Additionally, text extracts from the studies are qualitatively synthesised to investigate benefits and challenges of the use of SoSo. Results: SoSo is reported as being chiefly used as a support for collaborative work, fostering awareness, knowledge management and coordination among team members. Contrary to the evident high importance of the social aspects offered by SoSo, socialization is not the most important usage reported. Conclusions: This review reports how SoSo is used in GSD and how it is capable of supporting GSD teams. Four emerging themes in global software engineering were identified: the appropriation and development of usage structures; understanding how an ecology of communication channels and tools are used by teams; the role played by SoSo either as a subtext or as an explicit goal; and finally, the surprising low percentage of observational studies.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Giuffrida, Rosalba","Dittrich, Yvonne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382058"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["systematicmappingstudy globalsoftwaredevelopment distributedteams socialmedia socialsoftware computer supported cooperative work"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"empirical studies on the use of social software in global software development a systematic mapping study","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84877924399","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382058","identifier":[{"id":"84877924399","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-35d0cb3f-fce9-422c-a746-29394a0683f0"],"keyword":["systematicmappingstudy,globalsoftwaredevelopment,distributedteams,socialmedia,socialsoftware, computer-supported cooperative work"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3118E5CE8E4A23C3BC5C096E6B4FF5F5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosalba","key":"giuffridapau","last":"Giuffrida","name":"Giuffrida, Rosalba","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09505849","18736025"],"issn_org":["09505849"],"issue":"7","journal":"Information and Software Technology","pages":"1143-1164","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Information and Software Technology","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84877924399"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-35d0cb3f-fce9-422c-a746-29394a0683f0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Empirical Studies on the Use of Social Software in Global Software Development - a Systematic Mapping Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382058","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Software is created by people for people working in a range of environments and under various conditions. Understanding the cooperative and human aspects of software development is crucial in order to comprehend how methods and tools are used, and thereby improve the creation and maintenance of software. Both researchers and practitioners have recognized the need to investigate these aspects, but the results of such investigations are dispersed in different conferences and communities. The 6th workshop on Cooperative and Human Aspects of Software Engineering held at the International Conference on Software Engineering continued the tradition from earlier workshops and provide a lively forum to discuss current developments and high quality research in the field, providing both a meeting place for the community and the possibility for researchers interested in joining the field to present and discuss their work in progress and to get an overview of the field. Further dissemination of research results will lead to improvement of software development and deployment across the globe.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Prikladnicki, Rafael","Dittrich, Yvonne","Sharp, Helen","Souza, Cleidson R. B. de","Cataldo, Marcelo","Hoda, Rashina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384323"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cooperative Aspects of Software Engineering","Human Aspects of Software Development","Software Development Methods","Software Development Research","Software Engineering Communities"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cooperative and human aspects of software engineering chase 000000002013","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384323","ids":["itu-d04c1305-f4e0-4485-a074-39f5225b292e"],"keyword":["Cooperative Aspects of Software Engineering","Human Aspects of Software Development","Software Development Methods","Software Development Research","Software Engineering Communities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-89D0204A57596EADBA8DA4715EF6E9FA"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rafael","key":"prikladnickipau","last":"Prikladnicki","name":"Prikladnicki, Rafael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Helen","key":"sharppau","last":"Sharp","name":"Sharp, Helen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Cleidson R. B. de","key":"souzapau","last":"Souza","name":"Souza, Cleidson R. B. de","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marcelo","key":"cataldopau","last":"Cataldo","name":"Cataldo, Marcelo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rashina","key":"hodapau","last":"Hoda","name":"Hoda, Rashina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01635948","19435843"],"issn_org":["01635948"],"issue":"5","journal":"Software Engineering Notes","pages":"34-37","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Software Engineering Notes","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d04c1305-f4e0-4485-a074-39f5225b292e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cooperative and human aspects of software engineering: CHASE 2013","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384323","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This paper investigates End-User Development of Information Visualization. More specifically, we investigated how existing visualization tools allow end-user developers to construct visualizations. End-user developers have some developing or scripting skills to perform relatively advanced tasks such as data manipulation, but no formal training in programming. 18 visualization tools were surveyed from an enduser developer perspective. The results of this survey study show that end-user developers need better tools to create and modify custom visualizations. A closer collaboration between End-User Development and Information Visualization researchers could contribute towards the development of better tools to support custom visualizations. In addition, as empirical evaluations of these tools are lacking both research communities should focus more on this aspect. The study serves as a starting point towards the engagement of end-user developers in visualization development.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Pantazos, Kostas","Lauesen, Søren","Vatrapu, Ravi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-290259"],"event":{"end":"2013-06-13","place":"Copenhagen , dk","start":"2013-06-10","title":"The 4th International Symposium, IS-EUD 2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["End User Development","Information visualization","Visualization Tools"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"end user development of information visualization","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-290259","identifier":[{"id":"84884379175","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-9bc1a711-0bd0-4f63-be24-52505bc8f69f"],"keyword":["End-User Development","Information Visualization","Visualization Tools"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DF0B48E7AC25428E395C0527E5473946"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of IT Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kostas","key":"pantazospau","last":"Pantazos","locid":"fc9298d6-557b-4f3c-a005-7bed5d0cbe87","name":"Pantazos, Kostas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lauesenpau","last":"Lauesen","name":"Lauesen, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ravi","key":"vatrapupau","last":"Vatrapu","locid":"93ba7069-df22-46b2-bf4f-5eb53175ef75","name":"Vatrapu, Ravi","orcid":"0000-0002-9109-5281","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpedh","last":"Dittrich","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Margaret","key":"burnettpedh","last":"Burnett","name":"Burnett, Margaret","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"mørchpedh","last":"Mørch","name":"Mørch, Anders","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"redmilespedh","last":"Redmiles","